{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"734315500091342899","content":"\"I start with lighter ink, nearly water, and take down looser forms. Then I refine them with increasingly darker ink until I have my finished forms. Then I apply notes that keep my memory of the scene. I have heard tell of a magic called 'press-ti-didge-a-tation' or some such thing that may negate my need for ink but I have not had chance to test the theory yet and am worried it would not be as long lasting. These inks I make from anything that stains. The black is wood placed in a tin and then in a fire. There is a small hole atop the tin and when the smoke ceases to chimney from it the wood within is coal to be ground and mixed with water.\"","created_at":"2020-07-22T00:02:26.954000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"735285595672412191","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"734315500091342899","content":"(I'm i getting an actual lesson from an actual artist rn)","created_at":"2020-07-22T00:03:37.592000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"735285891949527131","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"734315500091342899","content":"\"Paper is the hardest to make and I most often splurge there as I like the smoothness the master crafters accomplish, prefering my texture to be created in process of the scriving.\"","created_at":"2020-07-22T00:03:47.333000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"735285932806111319","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"734315500091342899","content":"\"Most importantly, learn through play. Enjoy the doing and you will do it more and that will hone your abilities to merge with your aspirations. Often both will grow at similar speed.\"","created_at":"2020-07-22T00:05:10.240000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"735286280543404093","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"734315500091342899","content":"\"That growth is healthy even if it is at times frustrating.\"","created_at":"2020-07-22T00:05:35.280000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"735286385568907304","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
